Written Instructions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 The steps below are designed to coincide with screenshots you should need to take in order for your Milestone assignment (with minor exceptions).\
Step 1 | Change Ubuntu Hostname: Using the command below, rename your Ubuntu hostname to display the VM's name followed by your last name.\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 nmtui\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 2 | Update Ubuntu: After renaming the hostname of your Ubuntu VM, update the VM using the command:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'a0sudo apt-get update -y\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 3 | Upgrade Ubuntu Packages: Upgrade the software packages that are already installed on your virtual machine using the command: \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo apt upgrade -y\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 4 | Install Nano\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo apt install nano -y\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 5\'a0| Install Git\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo apt install git -y\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa530\partightenfactor0

\fs64 \cf2 \ul \ulc2 Apache\ulnone \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Step 6 | Install Install Apache Web Server Package:\'a0 Preparing to run an Apache web server, you will run the command below. This will include the "apache2" package, which should include all necessary files and configurations for running an Apache web server.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo apt install apache2 -y\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 7 | Create Firewall Profile for Apache: By running the following command, you will open up your VM's firewall ports so that TCP/80 and TCP/443 are allowed in.\'a0\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo ufw allow in "Apache Full"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 8 | Browse to Apache2 Default Page:\'a0 Test that you have installed your Apache software correctly.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 In your browser, go to 10.10.229.12\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa530\partightenfactor0

\fs64 \cf2 \ul MySQL\ulnone \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Step 9 | Install MySQL Server Package: Install the package needed to run a MySQL database.\
sudo apt install mysql-server\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo apt install mysql-server\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 Creating a snapshot of your virtual machine at this point is HIGHLY recommended. This allows you to revert to a snapshot prior to configuration should future problems occur.\cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 10 | Log in to MySQL: To begin initial configurations, log in to MySQL using the following command.\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo mysql\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 11 | Change MySQL Root User Password: You will need to change the password for the root user to access MySQL in future assignments. This identifies the \ul root \ulnone user. The semi-colon at the end of the command is required, as it indicates to MySQL you are finished with that individual statement (think of it as another word for a command).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 ALTER USER 'root'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED WITH mysql_native_password BY 'insert a random password here' ;\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul Note:\ulnone  You must document your MySQL passwords in your inventory in your documentation.\'a0 These passwords are not recoverable if you forget them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 12 | Flush Privileges: Instruct your MySQL server to reload grant tables from the disk.\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 FLUSH PRIVILEGES;\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 13 | Exit MySQL: Terminate your session of MySQL using the following command: \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 exit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa530\partightenfactor0

\fs64 \cf2 \ul PHP\ulnone \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Step 14 | Install PHP: The following command will install several packages crucial for setting up a LAMP stack.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo apt install php\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 15 | Edit the Sources.list File\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo nano /etc/apt/sources.list\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul Note\ulnone : Add "universe" to the end of all URLs in the file if it is missing.\'a0 Do not delete or replace anything in the file.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 16 | Update Ubuntu\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo apt update -y\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Note:\'a0This step is required to refresh the repolist\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 17 | Install Required PHP Libraries\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo apt install php libapache2-mod-php php-mysql\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 18 | Install PHP Extensions: WordPress requires additional PHP extensions, which extend PHP's functionality. \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo apt install php-curl php-gd php-xml php-mbstring php-xmlrpc php-zip php-soap php-intl\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 19 | Enable Rewrites in Apache: Enabling rewrites in Apache allows for "clean" URLs, which are often formatted more user-friendly.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo a2enmod rewrite\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 20 | Restart Apache: The changes you've made will take effect when you restart Apache.\'a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 service apache2 restart ("systemctl restart apache" may also work)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf2 At this point, you should have a functioning web server with the PHP language and MySQL database installed. Next, you will test to ensure that PHP is functioning correctly by writing a simple test script. This script will use a basic PHP function, something you don't need to be a PHP expert for. It's a handy trick to have in your back pocket when setting up web services.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
Step 21 | Create a Test Web Page: Here, you will create a new file in your html directory.\'a0 We'll call this file "test.php".\'a0 You'll use the following command:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 sudo nano /var/www/html/test.php\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Insert the following code and save your newly created test.php file:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <?php phpinfo(); ?>\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Step 22 | Test the PHP Test Page: Navigate to the Firefox browser on your Ubuntu virtual machine and load the test page. If you see the test page, you have completed the final step of this assignment and may move on to the next step.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf2 In the Firefox browser's address bar type: http://10.10.229.12/test.php\
}